Connect chemical-analysis results with sampling, standards, corrections, and material scale (@metal-chemical-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5", #source "../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME", #source "../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB", #source "../../../../stem/chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "../../../../inquiry/metrology/applications/Force-pressure-and-torque.lingua#r_20DYJT66R1TCW9M8X96TH7KGHT") { r_4A8HJMDKVC1V96HWB9DCX55H79
**Read:** [Measurement and metrology](../../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), reuse chemical measurement models, sampling, calibration, uncertainty, and method validation; [Metallography and Microstructures — ASM Handbook, volume 9](../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME), full relevant chemical/phase interpretation methods, when available; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), the complete relevant assay, impurity, and product-quality account; [General chemistry](../../../../stem/chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V), reuse chemical characterization and source-evidence methods.

After the shared microanalysis step, distinguish bulk composition, local phase chemistry, spatial maps, surface analysis, and dissolved/interstitial gas or trace-element measurements. Each method has a physical signal, preparation/standards, calibration/corrections, detection/quantification basis, spatial/support definition, and uncertainty.

A nominal purity claim or total analytical sum does not establish which impurities were measured accurately. Matrix effects, specimen heterogeneity, contamination, surface state, blanks, standards, spectral overlaps, and data processing can affect the interpretation. Results from differently supported samples or differently prepared states may legitimately differ.

Connect the consequential impurity/species and its phase location with the actual refining, transformation, corrosion, conductivity, or manufacturing question. Bulk concentration can be insufficient when local segregation, inclusion association, or a specific chemical state controls behavior. Preserve raw observations, method versions, and alternative explanations.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete alloy or high-purity chemical-characterization case using its full primary methods and reference-material evidence. Independently check composition/basis conversions and an uncertainty/calibration account. Compare bulk and local/trace observations with the expected material population, investigate a discrepancy, and propose a discriminating independent method. Explain exactly which product/process claim the results support and which remain unmeasured.

**Continue:** [Force, pressure, and torque — reference geometry and load history](../../../../inquiry/metrology/applications/Force-pressure-and-torque.lingua#r_20DYJT66R1TCW9M8X96TH7KGHT).

